{"type":"message","id":"53bea982","parentId":"d583676d","timestamp":"2026-04-27T11:40:25.863Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_process_eiy53Yclk5rijGAv2ODB","toolName":"process","content":[{"type":"text","text":"n crypto-related physical attacks\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"crypto wrench attack\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"France Charges 88, Including Minors, in Crypto ‘Wrench Attack’ Crackdown\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/88-people-charged-over-12-crypto-wrench-attacks-in-france\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365596/france-charges-88-including-minors-in-crypto-wrench-attack-crackdown\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"French law enforcement has charged 88 people in connection with 12 crypto 'wrench attacks'.\",\n    \"Some of the alleged offenders were involved in multiple incidents, and minors are among those charged.\",\n    \"France has recorded 135 crypto-linked incidents since 2023, amid a nationwide surge in these so-called “wrench attacks.”\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"France Charges 88, Including Minors, in Crypto ‘Wrench Attack’ Crackdown - Decrypt. France has recorded 135 crypto-linked incidents since 2023, amid a nationwide surge in so-called “wrench attacks.” French authorities have charged 88 individuals, including several minors, in a major crackdown on a wave of violent crypto-related robberies, known as “wrench attacks.” The arrests are linked to at least 12 separate incidents across the country. According to reports, these attacks involve physical violence or threats to force victims to transfer their cryptocurrency holdings. The defendants are accused of organized robbery, kidnapping, and assault. The investigation, which spanned several months, uncovered a network of criminals who targeted individuals known to possess significant amounts of cryptocurrency. Authorities noted that the rise of such crimes corresponds with the increasing value and mainstream adoption of digital assets. The French Ministry of the Interior has warned crypto investors to be vigilant and take extra security precautions, such as not publicizing their holdings and using multi-factor authentication.\"\n}\n```\n\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"nova-meadow","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"```json\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"French authorities crack down on crypto-related physical attacks\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"crypto wrench attack\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"France Charges 88, Including Minors, in Crypto ‘Wrench Attack’ Crackdown\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/88-people-charged-over-12-crypto-wrench-attacks-in-france\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365596/france-charges-88-including-minors-in-crypto-wrench-attack-crackdown\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"French law enforcement has charged 88 people in connection with 12 crypto 'wrench attacks'.\",\n    \"Some of the alleged offenders were involved in multiple incidents, and minors are among those charged.\",\n    \"France has recorded 135 crypto-linked incidents since 2023, amid a nationwide surge in these so-called “wrench attacks.”\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"France Charges 88, Including Minors, in Crypto ‘Wrench Attack’ Crackdown - Decrypt. France has recorded 135 crypto-linked incidents since 2023, amid a nationwide surge in so-called “wrench attacks.” French authorities have charged 88 individuals, including several minors, in a major crackdown on a wave of violent crypto-related robberies, known as “wrench attacks.” The arrests are linked to at least 12 separate incidents across the country. According to reports, these attacks involve physical violence or threats to force victims to transfer their cryptocurrency holdings. The defendants are accused of organized robbery, kidnapping, and assault. The investigation, which spanned several months, uncovered a network of criminals who targeted individuals known to possess significant amounts of cryptocurrency. Authorities noted that the rise of such crimes corresponds with the increasing value and mainstream adoption of digital assets. The French Ministry of the Interior has warned crypto investors to be vigilant and take extra security precautions, such as not publicizing their holdings and using multi-factor authentication.\"\n}\n```\n","name":"rm ~/.openclaw/agents/res...sessions/sessions.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777290025863}}
